Build the wheel with `full-dynamic`

Not from the upstream branch: upstream selects the feature set on the
maturin command line, which a PEP 517 build through pip does not reach.
`[tool.maturin] features` is where maturin looks when it is driven as a
build backend, so that is what has to name `full-dynamic`.

A substitution rather than an addition: `full` implies `link-static`, and
the previous patch makes the two linkage features mutually exclusive.
diff --git a/python/mq-bridge-py/pyproject.toml b/python/mq-bridge-py/pyproject.toml
index 3ded833..9f21a22 100644
--- a/python/mq-bridge-py/pyproject.toml
+++ b/python/mq-bridge-py/pyproject.toml
@@ -57,6 +57,11 @@ markers = [
 
 [tool.maturin]
 bindings = "pyo3"
-features = ["pyo3/extension-module", "full", "schema"]
+# `full-dynamic` rather than `full`: the same endpoint set, but librdkafka is
+# linked from the environment via pkg-config instead of compiled from vendored
+# C sources. The two differ only in `mq-bridge`'s `link-static` /
+# `link-dynamic`, which are mutually exclusive, so this is a substitution
+# rather than an addition.
+features = ["pyo3/extension-module", "full-dynamic", "schema"]
 module-name = "mq_bridge._mq_bridge"
 python-source = "."
